' /product/failure-propagation/ — a list of assets against a model of a plant.
' One pump fails; accent traces what goes with it. The unaffected branch stays
' muted on purpose: the graph is worth having because it tells you what is *not*
' affected as much as what is.
'
' Deliberately no standby pump on the lubrication circuit. Drawing one would
' imply the failure should not propagate at all, which is the first thing a
' reliability engineer would object to.
@startuml
!include theme.puml
left to right direction
' wider ranks so a horizontal chain fills the 860px measure rather than
' stopping two-thirds across it
skinparam ranksep 74

rectangle "Lube oil pump\nP-101" as p101 <<emph>>
rectangle "Bearing lubrication\ncircuit" as circ <<trace>>
rectangle "Compressor\nK-201" as k201 <<trace>>
rectangle "Train 2" as train2 <<trace>>
rectangle "Line A output\n<size:11>420 t/day at risk" as lineA <<emph>>

rectangle "Instrument air\ncompressor" as air
rectangle "Train 1" as train1
rectangle "Line B output\n<size:11>unaffected" as lineB

p101 -[#1E40AF]-> circ
circ -[#1E40AF]-> k201
k201 -[#1E40AF]-> train2
train2 -[#1E40AF]-> lineA

' Dashed, not just muted. The traced path is accent and solid, this one is grey
' and dashed, so the distinction survives without relying on hue — which matters
' for the blue-yellow deficiency the chromatic accent is weakest against.
air -[dashed]-> train1
train1 -[dashed]-> lineB
@enduml
